so `(M′-bf)` holds iff `Σ_i W_i χ̃_i + K_tot = N−1`, which given the Orevkov budget is exactly Lemma A. Every `σ_i`, `ν_i`, node count and crossing count cancels — on the companion as much as the branched component. REP-96 §7's `χ₂ + σ₂ = 1` is the `i=2` instance of `Σ_i W_i(χ̃_i−1) = 0`; it looked like a constraint on `D_2` only because Lemma A had already been spent on `D_1`. **`OPEN[REP-96-MPRIME-COMPANION]` closes NEGATIVE**: the identity cannot bind at any `N`, for any pinning of `D_2`. §2.4 diagnoses why the (H2) kill works — it runs on the *ceiling* `a ≤ N−2`, which Prop 2.4 licenses only on **branched** components, where it reads `W_i ≥ 2` and is automatic.

